Minato's patch to frameworks/base's media/java/android/media/Utils.java at android-15.0.0_r1 (Apache-2.0),
ADR-0060 e2b3, which MediaCodecInfo's ranges need: an audio device's address is never a Bluetooth one to anonymize.

Why: anonymizeBluetoothAddress asks AudioSystem.isBluetoothDevice, a native of the audio system, which is a
compile-only stub here (framework/stubs/types/android/media/AudioSystem.java). Minato has no Bluetooth audio devices,
so the address stays as it is, as Android leaves the address of a device that is not Bluetooth.

--- a/media/java/android/media/Utils.java
+++ b/media/java/android/media/Utils.java
@@ -683,7 +683,7 @@
      */
     public static @Nullable String anonymizeBluetoothAddress(
             int deviceType, @Nullable String address) {
-        if (!AudioSystem.isBluetoothDevice(deviceType)) {
+        if (true) {  // Minato: no Bluetooth audio devices (AudioSystem.isBluetoothDevice is the audio system's)
             return address;
         }
         return anonymizeBluetoothAddress(address);
